#!/bin/sh
# Install an XEMS mod from a USB stick while the machine runs (the XEMS panel's "Обнови от USB").
# Mounts the stick, runs its own updater.sh (backup + payload + remove.list, self-renames), reports.
# The firstboot hooks still run on the next boot, like any stick install.
#
#   check : print "ver=N installed=M"; exit 0 if the stick carries a different version (an update)
#   apply : install; print "OK <ver>" on success, else "ERR <reason>" (exit non-zero)
#
# Env (tests): XEMS_USB_DIR = an already-mounted stick dir (skip the real mount);
#              XEMS_OPT (installed VERSION dir, default /opt/xems); XEMS_USB_DEV / XEMS_USB_MNT;
#              XB_ROOT is passed through to the stick's updater.sh.
OPT=${XEMS_OPT:-/opt/xems}
MNT=${XEMS_USB_MNT:-/tmp/xems-usb}
installed=$(cat "$OPT/VERSION" 2>/dev/null)

mount_stick() {   # echo the stick dir, or fail
	if [ -n "$XEMS_USB_DIR" ]; then echo "$XEMS_USB_DIR"; return 0; fi
	mkdir -p "$MNT"
	for dev in ${XEMS_USB_DEV:-/dev/sda1 /dev/sda}; do
		[ -b "$dev" ] || continue
		if mount "$dev" "$MNT" 2>/dev/null; then echo "$MNT"; return 0; fi
	done
	return 1
}
umount_stick() { [ -n "$XEMS_USB_DIR" ] || umount "$MNT" 2>/dev/null; }

dir=$(mount_stick) || { echo "ERR no-stick"; exit 2; }
ver=$(cat "$dir/xems/VERSION" 2>/dev/null)
if [ ! -f "$dir/updater.sh" ] || [ ! -f "$dir/xems/payload.tar.gz" ] || [ -z "$ver" ]; then
	umount_stick
	echo "ERR not-an-xems-stick"
	exit 2
fi

case "$1" in
check)
	umount_stick
	echo "ver=$ver installed=$installed"
	[ "$ver" != "$installed" ]
	;;
apply)
	if ( cd "$dir" && sh ./updater.sh ) > /dev/null 2>&1; then r=0; else r=1; fi
	sync
	umount_stick
	if [ "$r" = 0 ]; then
		echo "OK $ver"
	else
		echo "ERR install-failed"
		exit 1
	fi
	;;
*)
	umount_stick
	echo "ERR usage"
	exit 2
	;;
esac
